NAME
    rmdir - remove one or more EMPTY directories

SYNOPSIS
    rmdir DIR [DIR...]

DESCRIPTION
    Removes each DIR. The kernel sys_rmdir refuses non-empty
    directories — any child entry whose parent_dir points at the
    target blocks the removal (POSIX ENOTEMPTY analog).

    For recursive removal, remove the contents first (with rm and
    rmdir) and then rmdir the now-empty container. There is no -r
    or rm -r in this OS yet.

EXAMPLES
    rmdir tmp
    rmdir /var/log /var/spool

EXIT STATUS
    0   every DIR was removed
    1   at least one DIR could not be removed (not empty, not a
        directory, missing, or no permission)

SEE ALSO
    rm(1), mkdir(1), find(1)

NOTES
    Same owner-or-root permission model as rm. Added in session 83
    via the new SYS_RMDIR syscall (= 86).
